WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.308 --> 00:00:06.809
The town clock was striking 8 p.m. when I arrived in Millcote on that raw October evening.

2
00:00:06.812 --> 00:00:16.955
No one from Thornfield was there to meet me, so I went into the inn to wait. After half an hour, I finally thought to ask a waiter for help.

3
00:00:16.956 --> 00:00:23.374
"Is your name Eyre, miss?" he asked. "If so, a person has just arrived for you."

4
00:00:23.375 --> 00:00:34.940
I jumped up, took my muff and umbrella, and hurried outside. A man was standing by a one-horse carriage. I stepped in and he hoisted my trunk aboard.

5
00:00:34.941 --> 00:00:41.273
Two hours passed before we drove through a pair of gates and arrived outside a large house.

6
00:00:41.274 --> 00:00:46.670
Candlelight gleamed from only one window; the rest of the house was dark.

7
00:00:46.671 --> 00:00:51.849
A maid opened the carriage door and asked me to follow her into the house.

8
00:00:51.850 --> 00:01:04.242
She led me to a snug room, where a little old woman sat knitting by the fire while a cat slept on the rug. I couldn't imagine a more reassuring scene.

9
00:01:04.243 --> 00:01:07.285
"Mrs. Fairfax?" I said.

10
00:01:07.286 --> 00:01:18.750
"Yes, my dear. Come sit by the fire. You must be cold after your tedious journey. John drives so slowly."

11
00:01:18.751 --> 00:01:25.496
Then Mrs. Fairfax said to the maid, "Leah, bring us some hot tea and sandwiches."

12
00:01:25.496 --> 00:01:31.723
Meanwhile Mrs. Fairfax went away to make sure that my luggage was carried to my room.

13
00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:37.548
When she returned, she cleared the table of her knitting to make space for the tea tray.

14
00:01:37.549 --> 00:01:43.212
I was confused by all the attention that my new employer was lavishing on me.

15
00:01:43.213 --> 00:01:48.122
"Will I have the pleasure of seeing Miss Fairfax tonight?" I asked.

16
00:01:48.123 --> 00:01:53.628
"Oh, you mean Miss Varens! Adele Varens is your pupil."

17
00:01:53.629 --> 00:01:56.023
"Then she isn't your daughter?"

18
00:01:56.024 --> 00:01:59.040
"No, I have no family."

19
00:01:59.041 --> 00:02:05.459
I found this perplexing but didn't want to be impolite by asking more questions.

20
00:02:05.459 --> 00:02:10.782
"It will be quite pleasant now that you're here," Mrs. Fairfax went on.

21
00:02:10.783 --> 00:02:16.684
"Leah and John are decent people and so is John's wife, Mary, who is the cook.

22
00:02:16.685 --> 00:02:28.426
But they're only servants, and one must keep them at a distance for fear of losing one's authority. Oh, here I am going on, and you're tired."

23
00:02:28.427 --> 00:02:34.417
As she showed me upstairs, I felt that the whole house was cold and cheerless.

24
00:02:34.418 --> 00:02:42.902
I was glad to find that my own room was warm and welcoming. After a long day, I had reached a safe haven.

25
00:02:42.903 --> 00:02:54.986
The next morning I dressed with care in my plain black frock. Looking in the mirror, I wished that I were taller and prettier, but I didn't know why I had these feelings.

26
00:02:54.987 --> 00:03:00.427
I went down the imposing oak staircase to the hall and out the front door.

27
00:03:00.428 --> 00:03:05.427
Crossing the lawn, I turned and looked back at the house.

28
00:03:05.427 --> 00:03:15.397
It was three stories high, large but not imposing—a gentleman's estate. Mrs. Fairfax appeared at the door and called to me.

29
00:03:15.398 --> 00:03:19.142
"How do you like Thornfield?" she asked.

30
00:03:19.142 --> 00:03:23.724
I walked up to her. "I like it very much."

31
00:03:23.725 --> 00:03:36.459
"It is a pretty place," she agreed. "But I fear it will start to decline unless Mr. Rochester decides to reside here permanently or at least to visit more often."

32
00:03:36.460 --> 00:03:41.450
"Mr. Rochester!" I exclaimed. "Who's that?"

33
00:03:41.451 --> 00:03:47.105
"The owner of Thornfield," she said, as if everyone knew that fact.

34
00:03:47.106 --> 00:03:53.096
"But I thought Thornfield belonged to you." Now I was truly confused.

35
00:03:53.097 --> 00:04:09.509
"To me? Bless you, child, what an idea!" Mrs. Fairfax smiled. "I'm only the housekeeper, though I am a distant relative of Mr. Rochester. His mother was a Fairfax."

36
00:04:09.510 --> 00:04:11.617
"And my pupil?"

37
00:04:11.618 --> 00:04:21.340
"She's Mr. Rochester's ward. He asked me to find a governess for her. Here she comes now with her nurse, Sophie."

38
00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:29.181
A small child of perhaps seven or eight ran up to us. Her long, golden curls reached her waist.

39
00:04:29.182 --> 00:04:36.086
"Is this my governess?" she asked her nurse in French, and the woman responded in the same language.

40
00:04:36.087 --> 00:04:40.011
"Are they from France?" I asked Mrs. Fairfax.

41
00:04:40.012 --> 00:04:47.757
"Yes. I was glad when you advertised that you speak French. I can't speak a word of it myself."

42
00:04:47.758 --> 00:04:57.313
We went into breakfast, where I conversed with Adele and soon learned that Mr. Rochester had brought her to England after her mother died.

43
00:04:57.314 --> 00:05:03.377
After breakfast Adele and I went to the library, which had been set up as our schoolroom.

44
00:05:03.378 --> 00:05:10.741
She was not used to school, so I taught her only a little that morning although I talked to her a great deal.

45
00:05:10.742 --> 00:05:19.885
At noontime I allowed her to return to her nurse. I decided to occupy myself until lunch by drawing some sketches for her.

46
00:05:19.886 --> 00:05:29.863
As I was going to fetch my paper and pencils, I saw Mrs. Fairfax in the dining room—a stately room with purple chairs and walnut-paneled walls.

47
00:05:29.864 --> 00:05:41.027
"What a beautiful room, and you keep it so nicely!" I exclaimed. "Except for the fact that the air feels chilly, one would think the room was used daily."

48
00:05:41.028 --> 00:05:48.114
"I like to have everything ready for Mr. Rochester, although he rarely visits," she explained.

49
00:05:48.115 --> 00:05:55.763
"But when he does, it's always at the last minute, and he doesn't like the bustle of cleaning going on around him."

50
00:05:55.764 --> 00:05:58.000
"Is he a fussy man?"

51
00:05:58.001 --> 00:06:00.605
"Not particularly so."

52
00:06:00.605 --> 00:06:03.356
"Do people generally like him?"

53
00:06:03.357 --> 00:06:12.076
"Oh yes. The family has always been respected here, though he is a bit peculiar."

54
00:06:12.077 --> 00:06:15.527
"Peculiar? In what way?"

55
00:06:15.528 --> 00:06:24.170
"I don't know. You feel it when you speak to him. You can't always tell whether he's serious or not."

56
00:06:24.170 --> 00:06:31.405
This made me feel curious about our employer's character, but Mrs. Fairfax said nothing more about it.

57
00:06:31.406 --> 00:06:36.484
When we left the dining room, she volunteered to show me the whole house.

58
00:06:36.485 --> 00:06:43.721
I followed her upstairs and down, admiring as I went, for all was well arranged and handsome.

59
00:06:43.722 --> 00:06:50.808
The rooms on the third floor, though, were dark and small and filled with furniture long out of style.

60
00:06:50.809 --> 00:06:58.618
All this—plus the lone window at the end of the corridor—gave that floor an air of gloom.

61
00:06:58.619 --> 00:07:06.539
Mrs. Fairfax led me up onto the flat roof of the house, which offered a fine view of the surrounding countryside.

62
00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:12.784
As I descended the steps to the third floor, she stayed behind to fasten the trapdoor.

63
00:07:12.785 --> 00:07:17.566
Suddenly I heard a strange, mirthless laugh.

64
00:07:17.567 --> 00:07:24.771
Startled, I called out to Mrs. Fairfax as she came downstairs. "Did you hear that laugh?"

65
00:07:24.771 --> 00:07:33.533
"Oh, that's one of the servants. Grace Poole sews up here, and she and Leah are often noisy together."

66
00:07:33.534 --> 00:07:38.843
Just then I heard the laugh again followed by an odd murmur.

67
00:07:38.844 --> 00:07:42.681
"Grace!" exclaimed Mrs. Fairfax.

68
00:07:42.682 --> 00:07:47.590
"Are you sure you don't have any ghosts in this house?" I asked nervously.

69
00:07:47.591 --> 00:07:56.004
"Quite sure," Mrs. Fairfax replied. "Come along to lunch, my dear."

